# Pull requests that moved shipped source and are cited in no changelog
# section, with the reason each one is excluded. Read by
# scripts/changelog-completeness.mjs.
#
# Format: <number>: <reason>
#
# A bare number is refused, and every entry that APPLIES to the release being
# checked is printed on a passing run too - an exclusion nobody can see is how
# a gate stops meaning anything.
#
# The five below are all from the 0.1.6 range. They are recorded here rather
# than written into a section that has already shipped, so that a run against
# that tag still reproduces green. From 0.1.7 on, the answer to a finding is an
# entry in the section, not a line in this file.

1982: 0.1.6 - converter-corpus coverage for Djot, BBCode and CommonMark structures, written up nowhere at the time. No clause and no fixture ruling moved with it.
1993: 0.1.6 - follow-up to carve#1990, which the section cites: it corrects the resolver-call-bound claim that entry describes.
2035: 0.1.6 - density edit of the clauses from carve#2030 and carve#2031. Every MUST, anchor phrase and constraint unchanged, no fixture moved.
2085: 0.1.6 - the part of carve#2084 an engine already agreed on; the section cites that ruling and the issue stayed open for the shape this does not reach.
2101: 0.1.6 - a fixture catching up with the carve#2091 ruling the section cites, which it predates.
